  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output A.1. More accurate and sustainable statistics on decent work using the latest statistical standards</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Based on the labour force module of the Household Income and Expenditure Survey, Vanuatu National Statistics Office in 2021 launched the Labour Market Monograph for Vanuatu. This Labour Market Monograph presents the analysis of characteristics of demographics, economic activity, and labour force of Vanuatu, as captured before the outbreak of the COVID-19 global pandemic and the effects of Tropical Cyclone Harold. Vanuatu was among the first countries to implement the labour force module, which is in line with the latest international standards on labour force statistics from the 19th International Conference of Labour Statisticians, and provides core data on the labour force. The Vanuatu household income and expenditure survey 2019-2020 microdata were then made available to the ILO, and the core-derived variables in line with ILO standards have been processed. Vanuatu requested ILO technical assistance in preparing a first draft of the Labour Market Monograph. The ILO provided technical support in:
(a) Outline of the labour market report and tabulation plan; (b) Report tables as well all graphs of the main report; c) Draft of the labour market monograph report; d) Final 2021 Vanuatu labour market monograph report ready for layout and publication.
The 2021 Vanuatu labour market monograph was finally launched in July 2021 along with other major reports from household income and expenditure survey 2019-2020, and as part of a series of the Vanuatu national sustainable development plan baseline reports. Consequently the ILO has also published detailed labour force statistics from household income and expenditure survey 2019-2020 into its global database ILOSTAT.</narrative>
   </description>
